		<title type="html"><![CDATA[How to increase the quality of physics for IPO baking ?]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=4161#p4161"><![CDATA[
I just committed the fix that enables increased simulation quality by subdividing the timestep. This should go in version 2.44 of Blender.<br><div class="codebox"><p>Code: </p><pre><code>import PhysicsConstraints PhysicsConstraints.setNumTimeSubSteps(2) </code></pre></div>You can also use higher numbers then 2 obviously.<br><br>Also the random seed used inside the simulation is now reset after simulation restart. So hopefully that makes the simulation more deterministic (one one platform).<br><br>Hope this helps,<br>Erwin<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Mon May 07, 2007 7:01 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
