See <a href="http://www.continuousphysics.com/mediawiki-1.5.8/index.php?title=Physics_Tips" class="postlink">http://www.continuousphysics.com/mediaw ... ysics_Tips</a><br><br>You probably need Blender 2.42 for this to work. Then attach a python script in the game engine, and run those lines:<br><div class="codebox"><p>Code: </p><pre><code>import PhysicsConstraintsPhysicsConstraints.setNumTimeSubSteps(2)</code></pre></div>You can increase that number for higher quality. Also read the other Physics Tips in above link.<br><br>After 2.43 we hopefully have time to improve physics baking, with more options as buttons.<br><br>Hope this helps,<br>Erwin<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Mon Feb 19, 2007 6:41 pm</p><hr />
